<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index fell 16 points to 1,310.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index fell 16 points to 1,310.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates fell to 1,310 today from 1,326 on July 25, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1420    12.894	  1428    12.964</p>
<p>   1a   1295  9806.000	  1315  9957.000</p>
<p>   2    1588    22.688	  1605    22.936</p>
<p>   2a   1552 12731.000	  1583 12986.000</p>
<p>   3    1458    13.450	  1479    13.643</p>
<p>   3a   1185  9350.000	  1212  9564.000</p>
